The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if ((status & IWL_RX_MPDU_STATUS_SEC_MASK) == IWL_RX_MPDU_STATUS_SEC_NONE)
    return 0;

if (!(status & IWL_RX_MPDU_STATUS_KEY_VALID))
    return -1;
```
Reason:
The first statement checks if the received frame has no security applied and returns early, effectively ignoring the beacon. The second statement checks for key validity and returns -1 if the key is not valid, which also leads to the failure of reporting beacon protection issues to userspace, causing beacons to be silently dropped.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
goto report;

wdev = ieee80211_vif_to_wdev(mvmsta->vif);
if (wdev->netdev)
    cfg80211_rx_unprot_mlme_mgmt(wdev->netdev, (void *)hdr, len);
```
Reason:
The `goto report;` statement allows the function to bypass the early return and proceed to the reporting section, where it communicates the beacon protection failure to userspace. The subsequent statements retrieve the wireless device and send the management frame to notify `wpa_supplicant`, ensuring proper handling of the beacon protection issue.

